        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7VRETilZOHFnB1T0Wc80-30" parent="1" style="shape=mxgraph.archimate3.application;archiType=square;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;appType=passive;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;" value="Not built (customer decision 2026-09-24): run summary notification,&lt;br&gt;dry-run property; the DONE log line and the import set rows are the report" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="50" width="360" x="1008" y="557" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7VRETilZOHFnB1T0Wc80-31" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;size=18;" value="&lt;b&gt;STRY0181133 - SAP actual costs into project expense lines (concept v2, DEV state 2026-09-24)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Question:&lt;/b&gt; actual costs from SAP in ServiceNow, mapped to the correct projects, monthly, the same way as the cost center file import.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Answer:&lt;/b&gt; the monthly SAP report is fetched from the MID server folder (transport, orange left), loaded into a staging table and transformed into one expense line per SAP order, cost element and period on the resolved project (mapping, orange middle); the OOTB rules roll the lines up to the project&#39;s Actual cost (green). Grey = platform records used as they are, yellow = data, orange = records of this story, red = not built.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Findings:&lt;/b&gt; the same load was done by hand in 2023 and 2024 (lines without key); the report carries the PRJ number in the Alfabet column and the SAP order resolves through the demand; the Excel loader reads displayed values (cents lost with a #,##0 column); re-runs update by key, unchanged lines are skipped, a changed amount updates the line and the project total at once (tested on DEV with the sample file: 17 rows, 11 lines, 3 runs).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;To do / decisions:&lt;/b&gt; D1 key order A-D, D2 cost plan assignment, D3 cost center granularity, D4 file scope and amount format rule, D5 historic loads (adopt the 2023/2024 lines by key, or start 2025), D6 folder on the MID server and the sender; end-to-end MID test; TEST, PROD." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="1940" x="-552" y="717" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
